.TH VDR-SUITE.CONF 5 "Phase 65" "vdr-suite" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite.conf \- configuration file for vdr-suite
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdr-suite.conf
is the planned configuration file for vdr-suite.

It will describe database, HTTP listener and VDR backend settings used by the daemon.
Until the file format is finalized, selected runtime settings are available as environment variables.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_DATABASE_PATH
Overrides the SQLite database path.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_RECORDING_ARTWORK_ROOTS
Semicolon-separated mapping of backend IDs to absolute local Recording artwork roots.
Each entry uses the form
.IR backend=/absolute/path .
For example:
.PP
.nf
VDR_SUITE_RECORDING_ARTWORK_ROOTS=default=/var/cache/vdr/plugins/tvscraper;wohnhaus2=/srv/vdr-artwork
.fi
.PP
There is no universal default. TVScraper accepts
.BR -d / --dir
and otherwise derives its storage directory from the VDR cache directory, which is distribution and installation dependent.
The configured root must therefore match the actual local TVScraper directory for that backend.

Duplicate backend IDs, relative paths and malformed entries disable local artwork delivery for the parsed setting.
A backend without an explicit mapping cannot use another backend's root.

Recording artwork references received from a backend remain internal.
The daemon resolves them only below the root assigned to that backend and exposes opaque, authenticated
.B /recording-artwork/
URLs to clients.
Missing roots, unsupported file types, invalid image signatures, oversized files and paths escaping an allowed root are rejected.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_VIDEO_ENCODER
Deployment default for the server-side video encoder backend.
Accepted values are
.BR auto ,
.B software
and
.BR vaapi .
The default is
.BR auto .
A backend-scoped managed setting stored through the authenticated Web/API settings surface has precedence over this environment value.
Clearing that managed setting returns control to the deployment environment and then the built-in default.
The choice is resolved for every new media session and remains stable for that session lifetime.
.B auto
selects only an implemented encoder backend with valid calibration evidence for the required workload and at least 1.25x measured real-time throughput; otherwise the required video transcode fails closed.
.B software
forces the existing x264 backend while retaining the typed x264 preset policy.
.B vaapi
forces the implemented VAAPI backend only when the required transformation and render device are available.
It may override the performance threshold but never a hard capability constraint and never silently falls back to software.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_VAAPI_DEVICE
Optional operator override for the private VAAPI render device used by the media worker.
The value must remain below
.IR /dev/dri/ .
It is not exposed through the public settings API or Web UI.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_PRESET
Server-side software H.264 transcode preset policy.
Accepted values are
.BR auto ,
.BR superfast ,
.BR veryfast ,
.B faster
and
.BR fast .
The default is
.BR auto .
Auto uses calibrated workload measurements when available and otherwise uses conservative typed software-preset defaults.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_STANDARD_PRESET
Optional override for ordinary HD-or-lower software video transcodes.
Accepted values are the same as for
.BR VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_PRESET .
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_DEINTERLACE_PRESET
Optional override for interlaced-to-progressive software video transcodes.
Accepted values are the same as for
.BR VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_PRESET .
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_UHD_PRESET
Optional override for software video transcodes whose source is larger than 1920x1080.
Accepted values are the same as for
.BR VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_X264_PRESET .
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_TRANSCODE_PROFILE
Overrides the measured media-transcode performance profile path.
The default is
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/media-transcode-performance.conf .
The profile is normally generated by
.BR vdr-suite-media-calibrate .
The daemon never benchmarks during playback or startup.
A media-session encoder decision is made before the worker starts and remains stable for the session lifetime.
.SH MANAGED MEDIA TRANSCODE SETTING
Authenticated administrators can select the backend-scoped encoder policy from the Web settings module or the corresponding
.B /api/backends/<backend>/settings/media-transcode
resource.
The managed values are exactly
.BR auto ,
.B software
and
.BR vaapi .
The API accepts no arbitrary FFmpeg arguments, codec names, device paths or process environment.
Read and modify permissions are scoped separately; browser mutations require the normal CSRF protection and accountability path.
The read model reports only sanitized policy diagnostics such as effective mode, calibration presence, threshold and VAAPI eligibility.
.SH MEDIA TRANSCODE CALIBRATION
The optional operator command
.PP
.nf
sudo vdr-suite-media-calibrate
sudo systemctl restart vdr-suite-daemon
.fi
.PP
measures representative software-x264 workloads and stores per-workload preset throughput.
Generated fixtures use a short benchmark duration.
Explicitly supplied real Recording references use a sustained 30-second sample by default and include source decode plus the normal AAC audio fallback when present.
The real-reference duration can be adjusted with
.BR --real-seconds .
Profile version 3 contains software measurements.
Profile version 4 additionally supports measured hardware-backend throughput and the VAAPI render device used for that calibration.
Versions 1 and 2 are intentionally rejected.
For x264 preset selection, auto chooses the slowest/highest-compression measured preset that reaches at least 1.25x real-time throughput; if no valid software sample exists, the typed software-preset fallback remains
.B superfast
for deinterlacing and
.B veryfast
for the standard and UHD-source software paths.
This software-preset fallback does not make an uncalibrated encoder backend eligible for
.BR VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_VIDEO_ENCODER=auto .
.SH LOCATION
The planned system configuration path is:
.PP
.I /etc/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8),
.BR vdr-suite-dashboard (1)
.SH STATUS
This manual page documents the current environment and managed backend-settings boundary while the final configuration file format remains under development.
